IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gdpr-core`
IMPORT `gdpr-core-2`
IMPORT `P2-seat-controller`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-cases-seat-controller.l4 -- cases for the questions of P2-seat-controller.l4, with the facts a real person in the seat would state.
-- Every case is a layer-1 case of notes/gen-tests-p2.py converted to the seat's inputs; its expected value was written by hand from the
-- text of the provision named in the comment above the group, before the first run, and none was copied from an output.  Where a
-- question has more cases in layer 1 than are shown here, the cases here cover every distinct expected answer.
-- ============================================================================


§§ `Article 12: transparent information, communication and modalities`

-- 12(1)a: Art 12(1) the controller takes appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language
-- all six requirements met; not addressed to a child
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- all six met, and the information is addressed to a child: 'in particular' stresses a case and adds no test
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no appropriate measures taken: 'shall take appropriate measures'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not concise
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not transparent
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not intelligible
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not easily accessible
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(1)b: Art 12(1) the information is provided in writing, or by other means, including, where appropriate, by electronic means
-- in writing
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I provided the information in writing, or by other means, including by electronic means where appropriate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- by other means (oral, say)
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I provided the information in writing, or by other means, including by electronic means where appropriate` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- by electronic means alone: an example of 'other means'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I provided the information in writing, or by other means, including by electronic means where appropriate` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- by electronic means, where appropriate
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I provided the information in writing, or by other means, including by electronic means where appropriate` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- in no form at all: 'shall be provided in writing, or by other means'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I provided the information in writing, or by other means, including by electronic means where appropriate` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- that electronic means would be appropriate does not supply the information
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, have I provided the information in writing, or by other means, including by electronic means where appropriate` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(1)c: Art 12(1) the information may be provided orally
-- requested by the data subject and identity proven by other means
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, may I provide the information orally` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not requested by the data subject: 'When requested by the data subject' (a failed 'When', ruling (b))
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, may I provide the information orally` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- identity not proven by other means: 'provided that'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, may I provide the information orally` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(1), as a controller, may I provide the information orally` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(2)a: Art 12(2) the controller facilitates the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22
-- the controller has facilitated the exercise of the rights
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(2), as a controller, have I facilitated the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the controller has not: 'shall facilitate'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(2), as a controller, have I facilitated the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(2)b: Art 12(2) the controller shall not refuse to act on the request of the data subject in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)
-- an ordinary request, not in an Article 11(2) case (the two Article 11(2) facts are false): 'In the cases referred to in Article 11(2)' is not met, the text is silent
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(2), as a controller, am I barred from refusing to act on the data subject's request in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- outside Article 11(2), and the controller demonstrates it cannot identify: still not covered
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(2), as a controller, am I barred from refusing to act on the data subject's request in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an Article 11(2) case, the controller has not demonstrated it cannot identify: it shall not refuse to act
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(2), as a controller, am I barred from refusing to act on the data subject's request in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an Article 11(2) case, and the controller demonstrates it is not in a position to identify: 'unless'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(2), as a controller, am I barred from refusing to act on the data subject's request in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an Article 11(2) case in which the data subject provided identifying information: the controller shall not refuse
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(2), as a controller, am I barred from refusing to act on the data subject's request in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the same, but the controller still demonstrates it cannot identify: 'unless'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(2), as a controller, am I barred from refusing to act on the data subject's request in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(3)m: Art 12(3) the months within which the information on action taken is to be provided
-- one month
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, within how many months must I provide the data subject with information on action taken on the request` FALSE EQUALS 1
-- one month extended by two further months
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, within how many months must I provide the data subject with information on action taken on the request` TRUE EQUALS 3

-- 12(3)a: Art 12(3) the controller provides information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of receipt of the request
-- provided on the last day of the month: 15 March to 15 April
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, did I provide information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of its receipt` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one day after the month: 'in any event within one month'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, did I provide information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of its receipt` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 4 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- provided on the day of receipt
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, did I provide information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of its receipt` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 31 January plus one month ends on 28 February (the month is short)
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, did I provide information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of its receipt` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 1 March is after the month that began on 31 January
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, did I provide information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of its receipt` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- extended by two further months: three months in all, last day
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, did I provide information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of its receipt` (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- extended, one day after the three months
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, did I provide information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of its receipt` (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 16 4 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(3)b: Art 12(3) the period may be extended by two further months
-- necessary, taking into account the complexity and number of the requests
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, may I extend the period by two further months` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not necessary: 'where necessary' (a failed 'where', ruling (b))
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, may I extend the period by two further months` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(3)c: Art 12(3) the controller informs the data subject of the extension within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay
-- no extension: 'any such extension' is not met, the text is silent
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, have I informed the data subject of the extension within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay` FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- informed on the last day of the month with the reasons
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, have I informed the data subject of the extension within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay` TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- informed one day after the month
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, have I informed the data subject of the extension within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay` TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 11 2 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- informed in time but without the reasons for the delay
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, have I informed the data subject of the extension within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay` TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`

-- 12(3)n: Art 12(3) the months within which the data subject is to be informed of the extension
-- 'within one month of receipt of the request': one month, with no extension of its own
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, within how many months must I inform the data subject of any extension of the period` EQUALS 1

-- 12(3)d: Art 12(3) the information is provided by electronic means where the request is made by electronic form means
-- electronic request, possible, not requested otherwise, provided electronically
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, have I provided the information by electronic means, where the request was made by electronic form means` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- electronic request, possible, not requested otherwise, but provided on paper
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, have I provided the information by electronic means, where the request was made by electronic form means` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- the request was not made by electronic form means: 'Where' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, have I provided the information by electronic means, where the request was made by electronic form means` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- not possible: 'where possible'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, have I provided the information by electronic means, where the request was made by electronic form means` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- the data subject requested otherwise: 'unless otherwise requested'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(3), as a controller, have I provided the information by electronic means, where the request was made by electronic form means` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`

-- 12(4): Art 12(4) the controller informs the data subject of the reasons for not taking action and of the possibilities of a complaint and a judicial remedy
-- the controller does take action: 'If the controller does not take action' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(4), as a controller, where I do not take action on a request, have I informed the data subject of the reasons and of the possibilities of lodging a complaint and seeking a judicial remedy` FALSE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- no action; informed on the last day of the month, without delay, with the three contents
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(4), as a controller, where I do not take action on a request, have I informed the data subject of the reasons and of the possibilities of lodging a complaint and seeking a judicial remedy` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- informed one day after the month
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(4), as a controller, where I do not take action on a request, have I informed the data subject of the reasons and of the possibilities of lodging a complaint and seeking a judicial remedy` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- within the month but not 'without delay'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(4), as a controller, where I do not take action on a request, have I informed the data subject of the reasons and of the possibilities of lodging a complaint and seeking a judicial remedy` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- no reasons for not taking action
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(4), as a controller, where I do not take action on a request, have I informed the data subject of the reasons and of the possibilities of lodging a complaint and seeking a judicial remedy` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- no mention of the possibility of lodging a complaint with a supervisory authority
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(4), as a controller, where I do not take action on a request, have I informed the data subject of the reasons and of the possibilities of lodging a complaint and seeking a judicial remedy` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- no mention of the possibility of seeking a judicial remedy
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(4), as a controller, where I do not take action on a request, have I informed the data subject of the reasons and of the possibilities of lodging a complaint and seeking a judicial remedy` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`

-- 12(4)n: Art 12(4) the months within which the data subject is to be informed of the reasons for not taking action
-- 'without delay and at the latest within one month of receipt of the request'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(4), as a controller, within how many months must I inform the data subject of the reasons for not taking action on the request` EQUALS 1

-- 12(5)a: Art 12(5) the information, communication or action is provided free of charge
-- no fee charged
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, have I provided the information, communication or action free of charge` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a fee is charged: 'shall be provided free of charge'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, have I provided the information, communication or action free of charge` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(5)b: Art 12(5)(a) the controller may charge a reasonable fee
-- manifestly unfounded or excessive, demonstrated, reasonable fee
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, may I charge a reasonable fee for a request that is manifestly unfounded or excessive` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the request is not manifestly unfounded or excessive: 'Where' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, may I charge a reasonable fee for a request that is manifestly unfounded or excessive` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the controller has not borne the burden of demonstrating the character of the request
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, may I charge a reasonable fee for a request that is manifestly unfounded or excessive` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a fee that is not reasonable or not based on the administrative costs is outside the grant, which the text limits by its own wording
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, may I charge a reasonable fee for a request that is manifestly unfounded or excessive` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- none of the three
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, may I charge a reasonable fee for a request that is manifestly unfounded or excessive` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(5)c: Art 12(5)(b) the controller may refuse to act on the request
-- manifestly unfounded or excessive and demonstrated
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, may I refuse to act on a request that is manifestly unfounded or excessive` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not manifestly unfounded or excessive
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, may I refuse to act on a request that is manifestly unfounded or excessive` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the burden of demonstrating has not been borne
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, may I refuse to act on a request that is manifestly unfounded or excessive` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(5)d: Art 12(5) the controller has borne the burden of demonstrating the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request
-- demonstrated
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, have I borne the burden of demonstrating that the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not demonstrated: 'shall bear the burden of demonstrating'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, have I borne the burden of demonstrating that the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(6): Art 12(6) the controller may request the provision of additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject
-- reasonable doubts, and the information is necessary to confirm identity
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(6), as a controller, may I request additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no reasonable doubts: 'where' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(6), as a controller, may I request additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- reasonable doubts, but the information asked for is not necessary to confirm identity: outside the grant
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(6), as a controller, may I request additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no reasonable doubts and not necessary
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(6), as a controller, may I request additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12(7)a: Art 12(7) the information may be provided in combination with standardised icons
-- information under Article 13 or 14
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(7), as a controller, may I provide the information required by Article 13 or 14 in combination with standardised icons` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- information under another Article: outside the grant, and the text does not say no
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(7), as a controller, may I provide the information required by Article 13 or 14 in combination with standardised icons` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 12(7)b: Art 12(7) the icons presented electronically are machine-readable
-- presented electronically and machine-readable
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(7), as a controller, are the icons I present electronically machine-readable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- presented electronically and not machine-readable: 'shall be machine-readable'
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(7), as a controller, are the icons I present electronically machine-readable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- not presented electronically: 'Where' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(7), as a controller, are the icons I present electronically machine-readable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- not presented electronically, not machine-readable: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(7), as a controller, are the icons I present electronically machine-readable` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`


§§ `Article 13: information where the personal data are collected from the data subject`

-- 13(1): Art 13(1) the controller provides the data subject with all of the following information
-- the data are not collected from the data subject: 'Where personal data ... are collected from the data subject' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, all of the information that paragraph 1 lists` FALSE FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- collected; no representative, officer, recipients or transfer; point (f) not relied on; points (a) and (c) provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, all of the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- (a) the identity and contact details of the controller not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, all of the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (c) the purposes not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, all of the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (c) the legal basis not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, all of the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- nothing provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, all of the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- whether point (f) applies is not answered (P1): item (d) is neither provided nor shown not to be owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, all of the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: not sure` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 13(1)i: Art 13(1) the controller owes the data subject the item of information
-- (a) the identity and contact details of the controller: owed in every case
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) the purposes: owed in every case
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) the legal basis: owed in every case
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(c) the legal basis for the processing` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) the representative: 'where applicable', and the controller has none
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) the representative: the controller has one
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` TRUE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) the officer's contact details: 'where applicable', and none was designated
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d): P1 does not answer whether the processing is based on point (f)
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(d) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: not sure` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 13(2): Art 13(2) the controller provides the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing
-- data not collected from the data subject: 'In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1' is not met, the text is silent
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, the further information that paragraph 2 lists` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a), (b), (d), (e) provided; no consent basis and no automated decision-making
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- (a) the storage period or criteria not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (b) the existence of the rights not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (d) the right to lodge a complaint not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (e) statutory or contractual requirement not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (c) 'where the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)': it is, and the right to withdraw consent was not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`

-- 13(2)i: Art 13(2) the controller owes the data subject the item of further information
-- (a) the storage period: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) the rights: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(2)(b) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d) the complaint: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(2)(d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (e) the statutory or contractual requirement: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(2)(e) whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, whether the data subject is obliged to provide the data and the possible consequences of failure` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) the right to withdraw consent: 'where the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)', and it is not
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(2)(c) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) the processing is based on consent
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(2)(c) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- data not collected from the data subject: outside the paragraph
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` FALSE `Art 13(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 13(3): Art 13(3) the controller provides the data subject, prior to the further processing, with information on the other purpose and any relevant further information
-- no further processing intended: 'Where' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(3), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- both kinds of information provided before the further processing
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(3), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- provided, but not before the further processing: 'prior to that further processing'
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(3), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- no information on the other purpose
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(3), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- no relevant further information
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(3), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- nothing provided, but the data subject already has both kinds of information (paragraph 4): the time is then immaterial
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(3), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- the data subject already has the purpose information; the further information was provided before
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(3), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`

-- 13(4): Art 13(4) paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 do not apply where and insofar as the data subject already has the information
-- the data subject already has the information: the paragraphs 'shall not apply'
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(4), as a controller, do paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 not apply because the data subject already has the information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the data subject does not have the information: the 'where' fails, so the paragraphs apply
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(4), as a controller, do paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 not apply because the data subject already has the information` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE


§§ `Article 14: information where the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject`

-- 14(1): Art 14(1) the controller provides the data subject with the following information
-- the data were obtained from the data subject: 'Where personal data have not been obtained' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the information that paragraph 1 lists` FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- paragraph 5 (b), (c) or (d) disapplies paragraphs 1 to 4: 'shall not apply'
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- (a), (c), (d) provided; no representative, officer, recipients or transfer
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- (a) the identity and contact details of the controller not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (c) the purposes not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (c) the legal basis not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- paragraph 5 not answered and items missing: the text does not say whether the duty was taken away
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: not sure` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 14(1)i: Art 14(1) the controller owes the data subject the item of information
-- (a) the identity of the controller: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) the purposes: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(1)(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) the legal basis: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(1)(c) the legal basis for the processing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d) the categories of personal data: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(1)(d) the categories of personal data concerned` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) the representative: the controller has none
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) the representative: there is one
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- paragraph 5 is not answered: it may take the duty away
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: not sure` `Art 14(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 14(2): Art 14(2) the controller provides the data subject with the following information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing
-- data obtained from the data subject: 'In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1' is not met, the text is silent
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the further information that paragraph 2 lists` FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- paragraph 5 (b) to (d) disapplies paragraphs 1 to 4
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- (a), (c), (e), (f) provided; no point (f) basis, no consent basis, no automated decision-making
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- (a) the storage period not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (c) the existence of the rights not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (e) the right to lodge a complaint not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- (f) the source not provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, have I provided the further information that paragraph 2 lists` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`

-- 14(2)i: Art 14(2) the controller owes the data subject the item of information
-- (a) the storage period: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) the rights: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(2)(c) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (e) the complaint: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(2)(e) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (f) the source: owed
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(2)(f) the source from which the personal data originate and, if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) 'where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1)': it is
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: yes` `Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) not owed: the processing is not based on point (f)
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): P1 does not answer whether the processing is based on point (f)
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: not sure` `Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 14(3)m: Art 14(3) the months within which the information is to be provided
-- (a) at the latest within one month: no communication and no disclosure
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, within how many months after obtaining the personal data must I provide the information` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 1
-- (b) first communication after half a month: at the latest at the time of the first communication
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, within how many months after obtaining the personal data must I provide the information` TRUE 0.5 FALSE 0 EQUALS 0.5
-- (b) first communication after two months: the limit of (a) is earlier, so one month
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, within how many months after obtaining the personal data must I provide the information` TRUE 2 FALSE 0 EQUALS 1
-- (c) a disclosure envisaged after a quarter of a month: at the latest when first disclosed
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, within how many months after obtaining the personal data must I provide the information` FALSE 0 TRUE 0.25 EQUALS 0.25
-- both: the disclosure is earlier
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, within how many months after obtaining the personal data must I provide the information` TRUE 0.5 TRUE 0.25 EQUALS 0.25
-- both: the communication is earlier
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, within how many months after obtaining the personal data must I provide the information` TRUE 0.1 TRUE 0.25 EQUALS 0.1
-- both: the disclosure is later than the communication and than one month
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, within how many months after obtaining the personal data must I provide the information` TRUE 0.5 TRUE 3 EQUALS 0.5

-- 14(3)a: Art 14(3) the controller provides the information referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2 within the time that paragraph 3 requires
-- provided exactly one month after obtaining the data: 'at the latest within one month'
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, have I provided the information within the time that paragraph 3 requires` TRUE 1 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- provided after one month and a half
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, have I provided the information within the time that paragraph 3 requires` TRUE 1.5 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- within a month but not within 'a reasonable period ... having regard to the specific circumstances'
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, have I provided the information within the time that paragraph 3 requires` FALSE 0.5 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) provided at the time of the first communication
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, have I provided the information within the time that paragraph 3 requires` TRUE 0.5 TRUE 0.5 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) provided after the first communication
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, have I provided the information within the time that paragraph 3 requires` TRUE 0.6 TRUE 0.5 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) provided when the data are first disclosed
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, have I provided the information within the time that paragraph 3 requires` TRUE 0.2 FALSE 0 TRUE 0.2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) provided after the first disclosure
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(3), as a controller, have I provided the information within the time that paragraph 3 requires` TRUE 0.3 FALSE 0 TRUE 0.2 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 14(4): Art 14(4) the controller provides the data subject, prior to the further processing, with information on the other purpose and any relevant further information
-- no further processing intended: 'Where' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(4), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- paragraph 5 (b) to (d) disapplies paragraphs 1 to 4
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(4), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- both kinds provided before the further processing
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(4), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- provided too late
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(4), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- no information on the other purpose
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(4), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- no relevant further information
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(4), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- unmet, and paragraph 5 is not answered: the text does not say
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(4), as a controller, where I intend to further process personal data for another purpose, have I provided, before the further processing, information on that purpose and any relevant further information` TRUE `P2 controller answer: not sure` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 14(5)a: Art 14(5)(a) paragraphs 1 to 4 do not apply where and insofar as the data subject already has the information
-- the data subject already has the information
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because the data subject already has the information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the data subject does not have it: 'where' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because the data subject already has the information` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 14(5)b: Art 14(5)(b) paragraphs 1 to 4 do not apply where and insofar as the provision of the information proves impossible or would involve a disproportionate effort
-- the provision proves impossible
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because providing the information proves impossible or would involve a disproportionate effort` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the provision would involve a disproportionate effort
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because providing the information proves impossible or would involve a disproportionate effort` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the obligation is likely to render impossible or seriously impair the objectives of the processing
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because providing the information proves impossible or would involve a disproportionate effort` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- research purposes subject to Article 89(1) alone: 'in particular' gives an example, not a ground of its own
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because providing the information proves impossible or would involve a disproportionate effort` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- none of the grounds: 'where and insofar as' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because providing the information proves impossible or would involve a disproportionate effort` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 14(5)b2: Art 14(5)(b) the controller takes appropriate measures to protect the data subject's rights and freedoms and legitimate interests, including making the information publicly available
-- point (b) applies and the controller took appropriate measures
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, where I need not provide the information because that proves impossible or involves a disproportionate effort, have I taken appropriate measures to protect the data subject's rights and freedoms and legitimate interests` `P2 controller answer: yes` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- point (b) applies and no measures were taken: 'In such cases the controller shall take appropriate measures'
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, where I need not provide the information because that proves impossible or involves a disproportionate effort, have I taken appropriate measures to protect the data subject's rights and freedoms and legitimate interests` `P2 controller answer: yes` FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- point (b) does not apply: 'In such cases' is not met, the text is silent
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, where I need not provide the information because that proves impossible or involves a disproportionate effort, have I taken appropriate measures to protect the data subject's rights and freedoms and legitimate interests` `P2 controller answer: no` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- point (b) not answered
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, where I need not provide the information because that proves impossible or involves a disproportionate effort, have I taken appropriate measures to protect the data subject's rights and freedoms and legitimate interests` `P2 controller answer: not sure` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 14(5)c: Art 14(5)(c) paragraphs 1 to 4 do not apply where and insofar as obtaining or disclosure is expressly laid down by Union or Member State law
-- expressly laid down by Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject, which provides appropriate measures
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because Union or Member State law to which I am subject expressly lays down the obtaining or disclosure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- laid down, but the law does not provide appropriate measures: 'and which provides appropriate measures'
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because Union or Member State law to which I am subject expressly lays down the obtaining or disclosure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not laid down by such law
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because Union or Member State law to which I am subject expressly lays down the obtaining or disclosure` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because Union or Member State law to which I am subject expressly lays down the obtaining or disclosure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 14(5)d: Art 14(5)(d) paragraphs 1 to 4 do not apply where the personal data must remain confidential subject to an obligation of professional secrecy
-- the data must remain confidential subject to professional secrecy
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because the personal data must remain confidential under an obligation of professional secrecy` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no obligation of professional secrecy: 'where' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 to 4 not apply because the personal data must remain confidential under an obligation of professional secrecy` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 14(5)e: Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4
-- point (b) holds
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do points (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph 5 disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- point (c) holds
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do points (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph 5 disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- point (d) holds
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do points (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph 5 disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: yes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none holds: 'where and insofar as' fails in each
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do points (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph 5 disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- none holds and point (d) is not answered: not covered
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do points (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph 5 disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- point (b) is not answered
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do points (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph 5 disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` `P2 controller answer: not sure` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` EQUALS NOTHING
-- point (c) holds whatever the others are
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(5), as a controller, do points (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph 5 disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` `P2 controller answer: not sure` `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: not sure` EQUALS JUST TRUE


§§ `Article 15: right of access by the data subject`

-- 15(1)a: Art 15(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller confirmation as to whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed
-- a data subject and the controller; Article 11(2) does not apply to the case
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I confirm to the data subject whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an Article 11(2) case in which the data subject provided identifying information: the articles apply again
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I confirm to the data subject whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Article 11(2) disapplies Articles 15 to 20: 'shall not apply'
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I confirm to the data subject whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the person is not the data subject: the grant is to the data subject, and the text is silent about anyone else
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I confirm to the data subject whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 15(1)b: Art 15(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller access to the personal data
-- personal data concerning the data subject are being processed
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject access to the personal data concerning him or her` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no personal data are being processed: 'where that is the case' fails (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject access to the personal data concerning him or her` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Article 11(2) disapplies Articles 15 to 20
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject access to the personal data concerning him or her` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- both bars
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject access to the personal data concerning him or her` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not the data subject
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject access to the personal data concerning him or her` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 15(1)c: Art 15(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller the following information
-- point (a) of paragraph 1: the right to the information, personal data being processed
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE TRUE `Art 15(1)(a) the purposes of the processing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- point (b) of paragraph 1: the right to the information, personal data being processed
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE TRUE `Art 15(1)(b) the categories of personal data concerned` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- point (c) of paragraph 1: the right to the information, personal data being processed
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE TRUE `Art 15(1)(c) the recipients or categories of recipient to whom the personal data have been or will be disclosed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- point (d) of paragraph 1: the right to the information, personal data being processed
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE TRUE `Art 15(1)(d) the envisaged period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- point (e) of paragraph 1: the right to the information, personal data being processed
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE TRUE `Art 15(1)(e) the existence of the right to request rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing, or to object to such processing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (g) the data are collected from the data subject: 'where the personal data are not collected from the data subject' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE TRUE `Art 15(1)(g) any available information as to the source of the personal data` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (h) there is no such decision-making: nothing whose existence can be obtained; the text does not say no
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(1), as a controller, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE TRUE `Art 15(1)(h) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 15(2): Art 15(2) the data subject has the right to be informed of the appropriate safeguards pursuant to Article 46 relating to the transfer
-- personal data are transferred to a third country: the right to be informed of the Article 46 safeguards
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(2), as a controller, must I inform the data subject of the appropriate safeguards relating to a transfer of his or her personal data to a third country or international organisation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no transfer: 'Where personal data are transferred' fails (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(2), as a controller, must I inform the data subject of the appropriate safeguards relating to a transfer of his or her personal data to a third country or international organisation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Article 11(2) disapplies Articles 15 to 20
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(2), as a controller, must I inform the data subject of the appropriate safeguards relating to a transfer of his or her personal data to a third country or international organisation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not the data subject
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(2), as a controller, must I inform the data subject of the appropriate safeguards relating to a transfer of his or her personal data to a third country or international organisation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 15(3)a: Art 15(3) the controller provides a copy of the personal data undergoing processing
-- personal data undergoing processing, copy provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, have I provided the data subject with a copy of the personal data undergoing processing` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- undergoing processing, no copy: 'shall provide a copy'
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, have I provided the data subject with a copy of the personal data undergoing processing` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- no personal data undergoing processing: nothing to copy; the text is silent
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, have I provided the data subject with a copy of the personal data undergoing processing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Article 11(2) disapplies Articles 15 to 20: 'shall not apply'
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, have I provided the data subject with a copy of the personal data undergoing processing` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- an Article 11(2) case with identifying information: the article applies, and the copy was provided
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, have I provided the data subject with a copy of the personal data undergoing processing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`

-- 15(3)b: Art 15(3) the controller may charge a reasonable fee based on administrative costs for any further copies requested by the data subject
-- a further copy requested, a reasonable fee based on administrative costs
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, may I charge a reasonable fee based on administrative costs for a further copy that the data subject requests` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a further copy, but the fee is not reasonable or not based on costs: outside the grant
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, may I charge a reasonable fee based on administrative costs for a further copy that the data subject requests` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the first copy: 'any further copies' is not met; Article 12(5) answers it
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, may I charge a reasonable fee based on administrative costs for a further copy that the data subject requests` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- neither
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, may I charge a reasonable fee based on administrative costs for a further copy that the data subject requests` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 15(3)c: Art 15(3) the information is provided in a commonly used electronic form where the request is made by electronic means
-- electronic request, not requested otherwise, provided in a commonly used electronic form
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, have I provided the information in a commonly used electronic form, where the request was made by electronic means` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- electronic request, not requested otherwise, not provided electronically
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, have I provided the information in a commonly used electronic form, where the request was made by electronic means` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- the request is not by electronic means: 'Where' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, have I provided the information in a commonly used electronic form, where the request was made by electronic means` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- the data subject requested otherwise: 'unless otherwise requested'
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(3), as a controller, have I provided the information in a commonly used electronic form, where the request was made by electronic means` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`

-- 15(4): Art 15(4) the right to obtain a copy is limited because the copy would adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others
-- the copy would adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others: 'shall not adversely affect'
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(4), as a controller, is the data subject's right to obtain a copy limited because the copy would adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no adverse effect: the limit is not engaged and the paragraph is silent
#ASSERT `Under Article 15(4), as a controller, is the data subject's right to obtain a copy limited because the copy would adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING


§§ `Article 16: right to rectification`

-- 16a: Art 16 the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller the rectification of inaccurate personal data concerning him or her
-- inaccurate personal data, a data subject and the controller
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I rectify inaccurate personal data concerning the data subject` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the data are accurate: outside 'inaccurate personal data'; the text does not say no
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I rectify inaccurate personal data concerning the data subject` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Article 11(2) disapplies Articles 15 to 20 (Article 16 is among them)
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I rectify inaccurate personal data concerning the data subject` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an Article 11(2) case with identifying information: the right applies
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I rectify inaccurate personal data concerning the data subject` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not the data subject
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I rectify inaccurate personal data concerning the data subject` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 16b: Art 16 the data subject has the right to have incomplete personal data completed
-- incomplete data, completion called for by the purposes
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I complete incomplete personal data concerning the data subject` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a supplementary statement is provided: 'including by means of providing a supplementary statement' is an example, not a condition
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I complete incomplete personal data concerning the data subject` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- incomplete, but the purposes do not call for completion: outside the grant
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I complete incomplete personal data concerning the data subject` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the data are complete
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I complete incomplete personal data concerning the data subject` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Article 11(2) disapplies Articles 15 to 20
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I complete incomplete personal data concerning the data subject` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not the data subject
#ASSERT `Under Article 16, as a controller, must I complete incomplete personal data concerning the data subject` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING


§§ `Article 17: right to erasure ('right to be forgotten')`

-- 17(1)(a): Art 17(1)(a) point (a) applies: the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed
-- (a) no longer necessary for the purposes
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (a) apply: the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) still necessary: 'where one of the following grounds applies' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (a) apply: the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 17(1)(b): Art 17(1)(b) point (b) applies: the data subject withdraws consent and there is no other legal ground for the processing
-- (b) consent withdrawn, no other legal ground
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (b) apply: the data subject withdraws consent and there is no other legal ground for the processing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) consent withdrawn but there is another legal ground: 'where there is no other legal ground' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (b) apply: the data subject withdraws consent and there is no other legal ground for the processing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) no withdrawal
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (b) apply: the data subject withdraws consent and there is no other legal ground for the processing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) no withdrawal, another ground
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (b) apply: the data subject withdraws consent and there is no other legal ground for the processing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 17(1)(c): Art 17(1)(c) point (c) applies: the data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for it, or the objection is under Article 21(2)
-- (c) objection under Article 21(1), no overriding legitimate grounds
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (c) apply: the data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for it, or objects to processing for direct marketing` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) objection under Article 21(1) but overriding legitimate grounds exist
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (c) apply: the data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for it, or objects to processing for direct marketing` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) objection under Article 21(2) (direct marketing): no test of overriding grounds
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (c) apply: the data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for it, or objects to processing for direct marketing` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) overriding grounds exist, but the objection is also under Article 21(2)
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (c) apply: the data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for it, or objects to processing for direct marketing` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) no objection
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (c) apply: the data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for it, or objects to processing for direct marketing` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 17(1)(d): Art 17(1)(d) point (d) applies: the personal data have been unlawfully processed
-- (d) unlawfully processed
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (d) apply: the personal data have been unlawfully processed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d) lawfully processed
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (d) apply: the personal data have been unlawfully processed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 17(1)(e): Art 17(1)(e) point (e) applies: the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law
-- (e) erasure required by Union or Member State law
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (e) apply: the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (e) no such legal obligation
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (e) apply: the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 17(1)(f): Art 17(1)(f) point (f) applies: the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1)
-- (f) collected in relation to the offer of information society services to a child (Article 8(1))
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (f) apply: the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (f) not so collected
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, does ground (f) apply: the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 17(1): Art 17(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller the erasure of personal data concerning him or her and the controller has the obligation to erase them
-- ground (a) holds, no exception
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, must I erase the data subject's personal data` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ground (d) holds, no exception
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, must I erase the data subject's personal data` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ground (f) holds, no exception
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, must I erase the data subject's personal data` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- all six grounds hold
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, must I erase the data subject's personal data` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no ground holds: 'where one of the following grounds applies' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, must I erase the data subject's personal data` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a ground holds, but paragraph 3 disapplies paragraphs 1 and 2
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, must I erase the data subject's personal data` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: yes` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a ground holds, and whether paragraph 3 applies is not decided: not covered
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(1), as a controller, must I erase the data subject's personal data` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: not sure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 17(2): Art 17(2) the controller takes reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform controllers which are processing the personal data that the data subject has requested the erasure of any links to, or copy or replication of, those personal data
-- made public, obliged to erase, reasonable steps taken
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(2), as a controller, having made the personal data public, have I taken reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform the controllers processing them that the data subject has requested erasure` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- made public, obliged to erase, no steps: 'shall take reasonable steps'
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(2), as a controller, having made the personal data public, have I taken reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform the controllers processing them that the data subject has requested erasure` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- not made public: 'Where the controller has made the personal data public' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(2), as a controller, having made the personal data public, have I taken reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform the controllers processing them that the data subject has requested erasure` FALSE `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- made public but not obliged to erase: 'and is obliged pursuant to paragraph 1' fails
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(2), as a controller, having made the personal data public, have I taken reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform the controllers processing them that the data subject has requested erasure` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- paragraph 3 disapplies paragraphs 1 and 2
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(2), as a controller, having made the personal data public, have I taken reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform the controllers processing them that the data subject has requested erasure` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: yes` FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- whether the controller is obliged is not decided
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(2), as a controller, having made the personal data public, have I taken reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform the controllers processing them that the data subject has requested erasure` TRUE `P2 controller answer: not sure` `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no steps and paragraph 3 is not decided: not covered
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(2), as a controller, having made the personal data public, have I taken reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform the controllers processing them that the data subject has requested erasure` TRUE `P2 controller answer: yes` `P2 controller answer: not sure` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 17(3)(a): Art 17(3)(a) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information
-- (a) necessary for exercising freedom of expression and information
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(3), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 and 2 not apply because the processing is necessary for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) not necessary for that
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(3), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 and 2 not apply because the processing is necessary for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 17(3)(b): Art 17(3)(b) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation or for a task in the public interest
-- (b) necessary for compliance with a legal obligation
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(3), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 and 2 not apply because the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation or for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) necessary for a task in the public interest or official authority
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(3), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 and 2 not apply because the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation or for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) neither
#ASSERT `Under Article 17(3), as a controller, do paragraphs 1 and 2 not apply because the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation or for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

